# QR-Based Self-Service Attendance System

## Overview

Implement a public-facing QR attendance page that allows gym members to scan a static QR code and mark their attendance using their Member ID. The page will be accessible via a Cloudflare Tunnel without requiring authentication.

---

## Your Idea Analysis ✅

Your plan is **excellent** and well thought out. Here's my assessment:

| Aspect | Your Idea | Verdict |
|--------|-----------|---------|
| **Cheap Domain** | For permanent Cloudflare Tunnel URL | ✅ Great - avoids random URLs |
| **Cloudflare Tunnel** | Expose specific page publicly | ✅ Secure - no port forwarding needed |
| **localStorage for Member ID** | Remember ID for quick re-scans | ✅ UX improvement |
| **Reuse existing attendance API** | Same validation/audio feedback | ✅ Code reuse |

### Minor Improvements I Suggest:
1. **Dedicated lightweight page** - Don't expose the main app; create a minimal `/qr-attendance` page
2. **No authentication required** - This page should bypass login
3. **Mobile-optimized design** - Since users scan on phones
4. **Optional: Auto-submit** - If localStorage has memberId, auto-submit on page load

---

## Architecture Diagram

```mermaid
flowchart LR
    subgraph Internet
        QR[QR Code in Gym]
        Phone[Member's Phone]
    end

    subgraph Cloudflare
        CF[Cloudflare Tunnel]
    end

    subgraph Docker["Docker Host (Your Machine)"]
        CLIENT[Nginx Client :80]
        SERVER[Express Server :3000]
        MONGO[(MongoDB)]
    end

    QR -->|Scan| Phone
    Phone -->|HTTPS| CF
    CF -->|HTTP| CLIENT
    CLIENT -->|/gym/public-check| SERVER
    SERVER -->|Query| MONGO
```

