### Component 4: Cloudflare Tunnel Setup

> [!IMPORTANT]
> This is infrastructure work done OUTSIDE the codebase.

#### Step 1: Get a Domain
- Buy a cheap domain from Cloudflare, Namecheap, or GoDaddy
- Example: `yourgymnameattendance.com` or `mygym.xyz`

#### Step 2: Point Domain to Cloudflare
- Add domain to Cloudflare (free plan works)
- Update nameservers at your registrar

#### Step 3: Install Cloudflared in Docker

**Option A: Run as a separate container (Recommended)**

Add to [docker-compose.yml](file:///c:/Users/Admin/Documents/Projects/escloop%20gym%20github%202/escloop/docker-compose.yml):

```yaml
  cloudflared:
    image: cloudflare/cloudflared:latest
    container_name: cloudflared_tunnel
    restart: unless-stopped
    command: tunnel run
    environment:
      - TUNNEL_TOKEN=${CLOUDFLARE_TUNNEL_TOKEN}
    networks:
      - escloop_network
    depends_on:
      - client
```

**Option B: Run on host machine**
```bash
# Install cloudflared
winget install cloudflare.cloudflared

# Login (one-time)
cloudflared tunnel login

# Create tunnel
cloudflared tunnel create gym-attendance

# Route domain
cloudflared tunnel route dns gym-attendance yourdomain.com

# Run tunnel (point to your Docker nginx)
cloudflared tunnel run --url http://localhost:80 gym-attendance
```

#### Step 4: Configure Tunnel Route

In Cloudflare Zero Trust Dashboard → Access → Tunnels:
- Create public hostname: `yourdomain.com`
- Service: `http://client:80` (or `http://localhost:80` if running on host)

---

### Component 5: QR Code Generation

Create a static QR code pointing to:
```
https://yourdomain.com/qr-attendance
```

Tools to generate:
- [QR Code Generator](https://www.qr-code-generator.com/)
- Or use any QR library

Print and laminate this QR code for the gym entrance.

